{"name":"Humble Gold","hex":"#edc796","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"humble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not pretentious or magnificent; unpretending; unassuming.","Having a low position or a low opinion of oneself; not proud, arrogant, or assuming; modest."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["People with a low position or a low opinion of themselves; those who are not proud, arrogant, or assuming.","An arrest based on weak evidence intended to demean or punish the subject."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humble"},{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Humble (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Humble\" is a song by American rapper Kendrick Lamar. It was released on March 30, 2017, along with its music video, by Top Dawg Entertainment, Aftermath Entertainment and Interscope Records. The song was written by Lamar and producers Mike WiLL Made-It and Pluss. The lyrics are a call to humility. It was provided to rhythmic contemporary radio as the lead single from Lamar's fourth studio album, Damn."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/58/Humble_kendrick_lamar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humble_(song)","wikidata":"Q29352319"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/HumbleSkrillexRemix-CoverArt.jpg/250px-HumbleSkrillexRemix-CoverArt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/HumbleSkrillexRemix-CoverArt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/HumbleSkrillexRemix-CoverArt.jpg/250px-HumbleSkrillexRemix-CoverArt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHumbleSkrillexRemix-CoverArt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4d/Kendrick_Lamar_Humble_Music_Video.jpg/330px-Kendrick_Lamar_Humble_Music_Video.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4d/Kendrick_Lamar_Humble_Music_Video.jpg/330px-Kendrick_Lamar_Humble_Music_Video.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kendrick Lamar dressed in all white in contrast to the black-clothed people lit on fire around him.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKendrick_Lamar_Humble_Music_Video.jpg"},{"srcset":"http